  "result": "I've written the revised record to `record.jsonl`. It fixes the gate's `UNUSED_CLAIM prim_heading_change`, but the gate hasn't been run on it yet.\n\n**The cause:** span d2 (\"shall not make a U-turn\") claimed `prim.heading_change` as an atom. The accepted concept `drv.motion.u_turn` already reads the heading change inside its own definition, and the gate doesn't count that as the rule using the claim. The only ways to use it directly were to repeat the concept's body or to add a condition that is always true. Neither is a faithful rule.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Span d2:** it now claims no atoms of its own and keeps only `drv.motion.u_turn`. The justification now says the concept carries the U-turn definition (DEF-NRS-484B-077) and reads the heading change itself.\n- **Assumptions:** the three entries keep their catalogue ids and no longer restate a `meaning`, since the catalogue already has ids with these meanings.\n- **Obligation text:** it now says the exceptions must hold for every school zone sign selected as in the applicability. This matches how the coder wrote the rule.\n\nThe other mappings, the occasion, the scenarios and the parameter proposals are as before.\n\nThe coder's run 4, with an always-true check added only to test the rest, returned `OK`. Their final files match that run apart from that check, so they should pass against this record.\n\nThe coder also noticed that the gate did not flag that always-true check as vacuous.",
